{"user": "Yeah, I was kind of looking at b7 too after typing in that response, what's the difference here between them and what White can do afterwards?  Keeping in mind I have never played this game before in my life lol and didn't even know it was a thing until now.", "user_ts": "2026-08-05T15:25:23.134324+00:00", "assistant": "You\u2019re comparing the right two.\n\nKey difference:\n\n- **After c8**, White can play the **a1 corner**: diagonal **a1\u2013b2\u2013c3\u2013d4\u2013e5\u2013f6\u2013g7** works for White. Corners can\u2019t be flipped back.\n- **After b7**, you flip **c7 through g7** to black, so that diagonal is broken \u2014 White **doesn\u2019t get a1** that way.\n\nSo even though **c8 flips more right now**, it may hand White a permanent corner. **b7 is about reducing White\u2019s dangerous replies**, not maximizing immediate flips.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-05T15:25:54.132802+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-05T15:25:56.003526+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question", "Metacomment"], "consensus": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question", "Metacomment"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 3, "Common Ground Question": 3, "Metacomment": 2, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 1}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 1.0, "Common Ground Question": 1.0, "Metacomment": 0.6666666666666666, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question", "Metacomment"], "sonnet": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question", "Metacomment"], "llama": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question", "Common Ground Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant": {"final": ["Direct Instruction", "Positive Feedback"], "consensus": ["Direct Instruction", "Positive Feedback"], "votes": {"Direct Instruction": 3, "Positive Feedback": 2}, "confidence": {"Direct Instruction": 1.0, "Positive Feedback": 0.6666666666666666